                    "One postcard showed the old railway station, but its caption named the town hall. The students checked the local archive and discovered that the image had been printed with the wrong label years earlier. They corrected the draft caption and asked the archivist to review the remaining cards.",
                    "The archivist confirmed three landmarks and could not identify two others. The students marked those cards as unidentified rather than guessing. Femi suggested that the unidentified cards could be used as a research challenge, inviting recipients to compare them with public history resources."
